  ============================================================================
  WHAT IS BUILT HERE, AND WHAT IS EXPLICITLY NOT
  ============================================================================
  BUILT: the body. "Colossal branching salt-crystal organisms, each rising
  from the deepest ultra-dense brine pools as a trunk five to ten cells wide
  before dividing into massive cubic and faceted limbs that climb upward into
  the lighter saline ocean." A body of "living ionic lattices." Sessile —
  "they cannot leave these abyssal pools" — so a multi-cell THING, never a
  PawnKindDef: it has no locomotion and it trades from where it stands.
  Placement is one per Grey Sea tile's deepest pool
  (GenStep_GreySeaFloorDressing, mandrake.rm.divinginteraction).

  🔴 UPDATE 2026-09-26 (same day, second FOUNDRY pass): THREE of the four
  owed mechanisms are now BUILT, in mandrake.rm.divinginteraction —
  RM_Building_BrineElder, RM_GameComponent_BrineElders,
  RM_ElderTradeUtility, Dialog_OfferToElder, RM_MapComponent_ElderDisturbance:
    1. THE DISCHARGE — BUILT. RM_Building_BrineElder ticks a visible charge
       (a spark tell past half charge) toward a rare unprompted EMP burst,
       and discharges immediately (any charge level) when disturbed — direct
       damage, or a pawn mining an RM_BrineJacket near its pool. One
       GenExplosion.DoExplosion(DamageDefOf.EMP) IS "stun living creatures,
       disable droids, collapse shields" — the exact vanilla EMP-grenade
       mechanism, MEASURED against StunHandler and CompShield's own EMP
       branch. "Cripple nearby ships" (Q8) is UNMEASURED and NOT attempted —
       filed as its own engine check, blocking none of the other three.
    2. THE NOVELTY TRADE — BUILT. RM_GameComponent_BrineElders persists a
       seen-set keyed by WORLD TILE (never by Map — a pocket floor map is
       culled once nothing keeps it home, so tile-keyed GameComponent state
       is the only thing that survives), and a separate per-world
       "one-of-each" flag for the RM_ singular treasures. Dialog_OfferToElder
       (opened from this building's own gizmo) is the trade surface — not a
       TraderKindDef. Valuation ignores market value and tech level for
       ACCEPTANCE (only whether the tile has seen this specimen's kind
       before); MarketValue only scales the payout size.
    3. DISSOLVING ITS POOL — BUILT, folded into the trade's reward delivery
       (RM_ElderTradeUtility.Offer): a successful trade destroys (never
       mines) one nearby RM_BrineJacket and spawns the payout in its place,
       or ejects the payout onto the pool's own margin if no jacket stands
       nearby — "ejecting long-entombed objects upward from the brine as
       part of an exchange", literally.
    4. THE RESONANT STORAGE CRYSTAL — STILL WITHHELD ON PURPOSE. "Growing a
       resonant storage crystal that passively increases the effective
       capacity or charge retention of all nearby batteries." MEASURED: no
       such comp exists anywhere in src/. ⛔ Not shipped as a def — a
       building with no comp is a decoration that lies about what it does.
       It ships with its comp or not at all. (⚠️ RUT_BrineBattery is an
       ANIMAL and unrelated beyond the pun.)

  Also still open, unchanged from the first pass: the "beautifully useless
  artifact" (needs a plot home first, per the sheet's own instruction — see
  RM_ElderTreasures.xml), the three canon treasures (owed to the Utinni patch
  layer per Q11a, not authored here), and offering a LIVE PAWN as a specimen
  (the sheet's "a colonist of a new xenotype is an offering" — a one-way,
  permanent removal of a colonist is not something to wire behind a single
  dialog click without its own explicit owner sign-off; Dialog_OfferToElder's
  header names this as a deliberate scope cut, not an oversight).

  ============================================================================
  WHY A SECOND COLOSSAL ORGANISM DOES NOT BREAK "ONE ENDEMIC GIANT LINEAGE"
  ============================================================================
  RULED ADDITIVE 2026-09-26 (content doc §8.2 item 1, sheet §4). The Elder is
  sessile, mineral and rooted — a formation that thinks, with no crèche, no
  locomotion and no lineage. The giant law is about the fauna line bred at
  the Miasma and returned here for its centuries (RM_Reefback). The Grey
  still has one giant ANIMAL; it now also has a geological mind, and the two
  never compete for the same niche or the same law.

  ============================================================================
  THE VOICE REGISTER, for whoever writes its text
  ============================================================================
  It "interprets history through chemistry, pressure, charge, mineral
  deposition, biological composition, and disturbance rather than names,
  politics, or technology." ⇒ An Elder reports WHAT CHANGED IN THE WATER,
  never who did it or why. It remembers "the Reshapers" — RULED 2026-09-26
  (Q9) to BE the Rakata, under the Elders' own exonym, not a new faction.
  They are the only eyewitness on the planet to the arrival.

  Trading with one should read as "negotiating with a geological intelligence
  that has spent tens of thousands of years quietly collecting one specimen
  of anything genuinely new" — not a price list. It is a strong candidate for
  the standing `claude -p` LLM text consumer, since it only ever speaks in
  chemistry.

  ============================================================================
  ENGINE NOTES
  ============================================================================
  size (7,7): the middle of his own "five to ten cells wide", and odd so the
  genstep can centre it on a basin cell. rotatable false (a 7x7 natural thing
  has no facings and no interaction cell).
  destroyable false + useHitPoints false: "preserved through catastrophes
  that erased younger civilizations" is not a hit-point total. An Elder is
  not something a raid removes, and making it mineable would turn the
  biome's mind into a salt quarry.
  tickerType Rare: nothing ticks yet, but the discharge and the seen-set will
  need one, and changing it later is a save-compat question best avoided.
  drawSize (11,11) against a 7x7 footprint so the limbs read as climbing up
  out of the trunk past its own base — his "limbs that climb upward into the
  lighter saline ocean" on a top-down map.

  PLACEHOLDER ART: the mod's own chimney placeholder, scaled up and tinted.
  Real art is owed and the brief carries the owner's aesthetic rule for this
  whole biome, verbatim: "marred slightly, don't make them too perfect or
  they look manufactured."
